{
 "quantity": "factor between Gaia DR2's unit weight error and the one this package simulates for a single star in the DR2 window, by G: the median UWE sqrt(astrometric_chi2_al / (astrometric_n_good_obs_al - 5)) of ordinary stars in a band of G over this package's single-star UWE in the same band",
 "sample": "gaiadr2.gaia_source, astrometric_params_solved = 31, bp_rp 0.90 to 1.55, astrometric_n_good_obs_al > 20, up to 5000 rows per band (the first returned by the archive; random_index < 200000000 from G 8), bands of 0.5 mag from G 4.5 to 19 and of 0.1 mag from G 10.5 to 12; the fit half of a band is its even rows and the held-out half its odd rows; nodes: a 0.5 mag band is cut into its 0.1 mag sub-bins when some pair of sub-bin medians of the fit half differs by more than 3 bootstrap standard deviations (validation/dr2/refit_factor.py), the node is placed at the median G of its fit-half rows (G_node), because the rows of a band with more than 5,000 stars cover only its lowest part, and the simulated single-star UWE of a node is the one of the 0.5 mag bands interpolated at that position; nodes: a 0.5 mag band is cut into its 0.1 mag sub-bins when some pair of sub-bin medians of the fit half differs by more than 3 bootstrap standard deviations (validation/dr2/refit_factor.py), the node is placed at the median G of its fit-half rows (G_node), because the rows of a band with more than 5,000 stars cover only its lowest part, and the simulated single-star UWE of a node is the one of the 0.5 mag bands interpolated at that position",
 "simulation": "wobbler.simulate_fit of a single star (a1 = 0, uwe_factor = 1) in the DR2 window, 300 draws on each of 60 seeded sky positions (Scan.from_position, seed 826); the median over the positions of the median over the draws",
 "bands_note": "band centres are the nodes of the linear interpolation; below the first and above the last centre f holds the end value",
